#' Effluent Limit Exceedances Search Service
#' 
#' @noMd
#' @param output Output Format Flag.  Enter one of the following keywords:
#' - JSON = Data model formatted as Javascript Object Notation (default).
#' - XML = Data model formatted as Extensible Markup Language.
#' - CSV = Results formatted as comma delimited file download.
#' @param download Name of data object to be downloaded, e.g., TopWatersheds, TopSIC, TopFacilities, TopPollutantPounds, TopPollutantTWPE, TopWatershedPounds, TopWatershedTWPE, TopSICPounds, TopSICTWPE, TopFacilityPounds, TopFacilityTWPE. NOTE: Use TopWatersheds, TopSIC, or TopFacilities in combination with the search parameters p_cas, p_poll_name, or p_poll_cat.
#' @param p_cas Chemical Abstracts Service (CAS) Registry Number.
#' @param p_co Facility County Filter. Provide a single county name in combination with a state value provided via p_st.
#' @param p_ct Facility City Filter. Enter a single case-insensitive city name to filter results.
#' @param p_dmr_tri_link DMR facility links to TRI ID Flag. Provide a Y or N to restrict results to DMR facilities that do or do not link to TRI ID(s).
#' @param p_dmr_tri_release DMR facility links to TRI ID(s) that reports releases to surface waters flag. Provide Y or N to restrict results to DMR facilities that do or do not link to TRI ID(s) that report releases to surface waters.
#' @param p_end_year End of Year Range.  Provide a year value in YYYY format to specifcy the last year to include in results.  Parameter p_start_year must also be populated when using this parameter.
#' @param p_esa ESA-listed species flag. Provide Y or N to restrict results to DMR facilities that do or do not discharge to counties w/ ESA-listed species
#' @param p_exceed_count Mininum number of exceedances. Provide a whole number greater than zero to limit the search to a minimum number of effuent exceedances.
#' @param p_exceed_scope Scope of exceedances to include in minimum count. Provide a coded value to filter results.
#' - FAC = Count exceedances across entire facilitiy
#' - OUTFALL = Count exceedances for any single facility outfall.
#' @param p_exceed_type Any Exceedance or Only SNC Exceedances. Provide a coded value to filter results.
#' - ANY = Filter on all exceedances 
#' - SNC = only those in which the permit is considered in Significant Noncompliance (SNC).
#' @param p_fname Facility Name Filter. Enter a full or partial facility name to restrict results. 
#' @param p_huc 2-, 4-, 6-, or 8-character watershed code. May contain multiple comma-separated values.
#' @param p_imp_poll Discharge pollutants contributing to impairment flag. Provide Y or N to restrict results to DMR facilities that discharge pollutants contributing to a waterbody impairment
#' @param p_imp_water Discharge to impaired waterbodies flag. Provide Y or N to restrict results to DMR facilities that discharge to impaired waterbodies.
#' @param p_lbs_exceed Limit results to facilities based on a specific amount (in lb) of exceedances of NPDES permit limits. Provide when p_exceed=Y is used. Cannot be combined with p_pct_exceed.
#' @param p_maj Major Facility Flag.  Enter Y to restrict results to Major facilities only.
#' @param p_naics North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) Filter. Enter two to six digits to filter results to facilities having matching NAICS codes. Digits less than six will match to all codes beginning with the provided values.
#' @param p_naics2 North American Industry Classification System Filter. Enter two digit code to filter results to facilities having matching NAICS codes.  A final wild-card is always present allowing "22" to match all NAICS codes beginning with 22. 
#' @param p_pct_exceed Limit results to facilities based on a specific percentage of exceedances of NPDES permit limits. Provide when p_exceed=Y is used. Cannot be combined with p_lbs_exceed.
#' @param p_permit_id Facility identifier from one of the following EPA facility systems: National Pollutant Discharge Elimination System (NPDES) ID, Facility Registry Service (FRS) ID, Toxics Release Inventory (TRI) ID, or Clean Watersheds Needs Survey (CWNS) ID.
#' @param p_permit_type Permit classification in ICIS-NPDES. Provide a coded value.
#' - NPD = NPDES Individual Permit
#' - NGP = NPDES Master General Permit
#' - GPC = General Permit Covered Facility
#' @param p_poll_cat Pollutant Category. Provide a keyword to limit results.
#' - NutN = Nitrogen
#' - NutP = Phosphorus
#' - ORG = Organic Enrichment
#' - SS = Solids
#' - MET = Metals
#' - PP = Clean Water Act Priority Pollutants
#' - CER = CERCLA Hazardous Substances
#' - TRI = TRI Chemicals
#' - RAD = Radionuclides 
#' - PAT = Pathogen Indicators
#' - Temp = Temperature
#' - WW = Wastewater Flow
#' - GRAD = General Radioactivity
#' - CLR = Color
#' - WET = Whole Effluent Toxicity
#' - PFAS = Per- and Polyfluoroalkyl Substances (PFAS)
#' @param p_poll_name Pollutant Name. Provide a single pollutant name to restrict results.
#' @param p_potw Publicly-Owned Treatment Works (POTW) Flag. Provide Y to restrict results to POTWs.
#' @param p_psc EPA Effluent Guidelines Point Source Category.
#' @param p_reg EPA Region Filter. Provide a single value of 01 through 10 to restrict results to a single EPA region.
#' @param p_qc_flag QC Flag. A Y value limits results to loads that have been flagged as potential outliers or data errors.
#' @param p_sic Standard Industrial Classification (SIC) Code Filter. Enter a single 4-digit SIC Code to filter results. If more complex filtering is required, use p_sic2 and p_sic4.
#' @param p_sic2 Standard Industrial Classification (SIC) Code Filter Alternate 2. Enter a wild-card search against SIC codes.  A final wild-card is always present allowing "22" to match all SIC codes beginning with 22.  Use the "\%" character within strings to match any SIC values with the pattern.  For example, "2\%21" matches 2021, 2121, 2221, etc.
